{
  "tema": 5140,
  "slug": "pronombres-infinitivo-gerundio",
  "titulo": "Pronouns with infinitives, gerunds and affirmative commands",
  "subtitulo": "Voy a escribirla / La voy a escribir. ¡Dámelo!",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "With a conjugated verb + infinitive or gerund, pronouns go either in front of the whole phrase or attached to the end of the infinitive/gerund (la voy a escribir = voy a escribirla), never in the middle. With affirmative commands they must be attached: dámelo.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When a conjugated verb is followed by an **infinitive** or a **gerund** (**voy a escribir**, **estoy cantando**, **quiero invitar**), you have **two** equally correct places for the pronouns:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "1. in front of the whole phrase",
              "texto": "**La voy a escribir.** **La estoy cantando.**"
            },
            {
              "forma": "2. attached to the end",
              "texto": "**Voy a escribirla.** **Estoy cantándola.**"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Never in the middle, between the two verbs."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When you attach pronouns to a gerund, or two pronouns to an infinitive, add a written **accent** to keep the stress where it was: **cantándola**, **comprárselos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the pronoun can wait at the door or ride on the back, but it never sits in the middle."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿No te ha llegado la carta? Seguro que ==la== va a escribir mañana.",
              "en": "Hasn't the letter arrived? I'm sure she'll write it tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "es": "Seguro que va a escribir==la== mañana.",
              "en": "I'm sure she'll write it tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Estás cantando tu canción favorita? —Sí, ==la== estoy cantando.",
              "en": "—Are you singing your favorite song? —Yes, I'm singing it."
            },
            {
              "es": "Sí, estoy cantándo==la==.",
              "en": "Yes, I'm singing it."
            },
            {
              "es": "Es el cumpleaños de Joaquín. Tengo que mandar==le== una tarjeta.",
              "en": "It's Joaquín's birthday. I have to send him a card."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Le== tengo que mandar una tarjeta.",
              "en": "I have to send him a card."
            },
            {
              "es": "Rafa y Luis son buena onda. ==Los== quiero invitar a mi fiesta.",
              "en": "Rafa and Luis are cool. I want to invite them to my party."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mandatos",
      "titulo": "Affirmative commands",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With an **affirmative** command, pronouns **must** be attached to the end. They can't go in front:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Los bistecs ya están listos. ¡Cóman==los== ya!",
              "en": "The steaks are ready. Eat them now!"
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Llevo los libros? —Sí, tráe==los==, por favor.",
              "en": "—Shall I bring the books? —Yes, please bring them."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡Da==me== las llaves!",
              "en": "Give me the keys!"
            },
            {
              "es": "Muéstra==le== el camino.",
              "en": "Show him the way."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Negative commands go the other way, in front: **no los comas**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dos",
      "titulo": "Two pronouns",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Indirect first, direct second, and always **together**:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Quiere comprár==selos==.",
              "en": "She wants to buy them for him."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se los== quiere comprar.",
              "en": "She wants to buy them for him."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡Cómpra==selos==!",
              "en": "Buy them for him!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Quiere se los comprar."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Se los quiere comprar. / Quiere comprárselos."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Never in the middle."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Los quiere comprar se."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Se los quiere comprar."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Keep them together."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¡Las dame!"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¡Dámelas!"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Affirmative command: attached."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Estoy cantandola."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Estoy cantándola."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Add the accent."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parientes",
      "titulo": "Related rules",
      "bloques": [
        {
